          %h2#FormalizationText Formalization in Categorical logic / in Modal homotopy type theory
          %p
            We introduce and survey here the formalization of Hegel’s Logic in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Science+of+Logic#nPOVRemark"} above remark
          %p We survey the matching of the formalization to Hegel’s text in.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#FormalizationDictionary"} Formalization dictionary
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#OverviewOfTheFormalizationProcess"} Survey diagram
          %p All this appears below in three stages,
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                in the Seinslogik at around
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#714"} §714
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %li
              %p
                then “reflected” in the Wesenslogik around
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#989"} §989
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
                and where every modality
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
                now has a “reflection”
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ′
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 'Mod'
                in the type universe;
            %li
              %p
                then “externalized” in Nature, given by a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                of this
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
                on a particular
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} (infinity,1)-topos
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
                has a representation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(Mod)
                as an actual
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-comonad"} (infinity,1)-comonad
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %h4#FormalizationConcepts Subjectivity
          %h5#ConceptFormalization Concept
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} Homotopy type theory
            as such (
            %a{:href => "#UFP13"}> UFP 13
            ) is a logic of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MartinLoef73"} Martin-Löf 73, 1.1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MartinLoef90"} Martin-Löf 90, p.1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MartinLoef93"} Martin-Löf 93
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Primiero08"} Primiero 08
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Asher11"} Asher 11
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#LadymanPresnel14"} Ladyman &amp; Presnel 14
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Sale77"} Sale 77, p. 6
          %p
            With the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/homotopytypetheory/show/universe"} weakly Tarskian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universes"} type universes
            included – which says that this essence appears properly reflected within itself – then its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interpretation"} interpretation
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            is in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} elementary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"} homotopy toposes
            (
            %a{:href => "#Shulman12a"}> Shulman 12a
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman12b"} Shulman 12b
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman14"} Shulman 14
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            of homotopy type theory. Conversely, homotopy type theory is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"} homotopy toposes
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory"} relation between type theory and category theory
            for more background on this.
          %p
            Accordingly, since it is more immediately readable, we display mostly categorical expressions in the following, instead of the pure type theoretic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
          %h5#JudgementInFormalization Judgement
          %p
            The earliest formulation of a logic of concepts is arguably
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aristotle%27s+logic"} Aristotle's logic
          %p
            Formalizations of Aristotle’s logic in categorical logic or type theory has previously been proposed in (
            %a{:href => "#PalmeReyesMacnamaraReyes94"}> LaPalmeReyes-Macnamara-Reyes 94, 2.3
            ) and in (
            %a{:href => "#Pagnan10"}> Pagnan 10, def. 3.1
            ). The formalization below agrees with these proposal in the identification of the Aristotlean judgement “All
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vdash f \colon B\to A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syllogisms"} syllogisms
            with composition of such function terms.
          %p
            %strong
              All
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a concept, a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgement"} judgement
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c \colon C
          %p
            says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            is an instance of the concept
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
            of type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            For instance if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            is the concept of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \colon \mathbb{N}
            says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is a natural number. Clearly here the “concept”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            may just as well be thought of as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of all its instances.
          %p
            Given concepts/types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            this is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
          %p
            The judgement that there is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            of the concept of functions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f \colon B \longrightarrow A
          %p
            says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a rule that takes instances/terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            to instances/terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon B \hookrightarrow A
            (so that the corresponding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\colon A \vdash f^{-1}(a)
            is a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            witnesses the fact that
          %blockquote
            %p
              All instances of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              are instances of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p or for short just
          %blockquote
            %p
              All
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              are
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            hence that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is das
            = succeed "llgemeine" do
              %strong A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is das
            = succeed "esondere" do
              %strong B
          %p
            This formalization of Aristotle’s “All
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            has been proposed in (
            %a{:href => "#PalmeReyesMacnamaraReyes94"}> LaPalmeReyes-Macnamara-Reyes 94, 2.3
            ), where it is attributed to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"} William Lawvere
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Pagnan10"} Pagnan 10, def. 3.1
          %p
            Notice that the choice of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            here is an important part of the formalization that is missing in Aristotle’s informal logic, causing ambiguity there.
          %p
            For instance, all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            inclusions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}\hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            realizing this. For the purposes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            these choices correspond to the choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
            (see the discussion there).
          %p
            Similarly, once we have that the informal “All
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            First, the meanings of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            may depend on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are to be taken as
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+types"} dependent types
            %em
              All
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is expressed by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            over the function type formed in context
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f\colon \underset{C}{\prod} (B \longrightarrow A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Second, even if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is not a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            it still expresses the fact that for every instance of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            there is a corresponding instance of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated+objects+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} n-truncated morphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28epi%2C+mono%29+factorization+system"} (epi, mono) factorization system
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+0-types"} homotopy 0-types
            refines to a tower of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n-connected%2C+n-truncated%29+factorization+system"} (n-epi, n-mono) factorization systems
            for all natural numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            %strong
              Individual
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            There is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E = \ast
          %p
            of which there is a unique instance, das
            = succeed "inzelne" do
              %strong E
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/being"} being
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            just purely are, there is no distinction and hence there is a unique instance.
          %p
            Hence a function of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \longrightarrow B
            is equivalently an instance/term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %blockquote
            %p
              The individual
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              is an instance of the general concept
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p or for short just
          %blockquote
            %p
              Individual
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            There is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            to itself.
          %p
            The single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/introduction+rule"} introduction rule
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            gives for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the statement that there is indeed an instance of this concept
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  r_b \colon b = b
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b = b)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi b
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_b B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
            via the constant loop
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi b
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_n \colon \ast \to \Omega_b B
          %p
            Under composition of loops, this object canonically carries the structure of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"} infinity-group
          #LoopingDeloopingTheorem.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              In any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} homotopy topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+objects"} loop space objects
              constitutes an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (infinity,1)-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi Ω
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Grp(\mathbf{H})
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\Omega}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{\mathbf{B}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\mathbf{H}^{\ast/}_{\geq 1}
            %p
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groups"} infinity-groups
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} connected
              objects in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p
            The inverse equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
            is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
            for more.
          %p
            Now in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            and in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} elementary (infinity,1)-toposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groups"} infinity-groups
            as grouplike
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+algebras"} A-infinity algebras
            is not available, since the latter is not a finitary concept. But by prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LoopingDeloopingTheorem"}
            the concept also has a simple finitary equivalent incarnation, which is available in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %em identify
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"} infinity-group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with its pointed connected delooping type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            Indeed this is most useful: homotopy type theory in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-representation"} infinity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
                in terms of
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles+--+theory%2C+presentations+and+applications"}> FSS 12 I, exmp. 4.4
              ):
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+type"} pointed
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+homotopy+type"} connected
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
