                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo ♯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643; \dashv \flat \dashv \sharp
            means that types carry
            = succeed "." do
              %em gauge measure
          %p
            From the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theoretic
            perspective the
            = succeed "-moment" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+infinity-connections"} flat infinity-connections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\flat}
            moment is that exhibited by infinity-connections given by just differential form data. For
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            etc. this is the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"}> rational
            ” aspect.
