              %em small path
          %p
            Accordingly, what were
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+infinity-stacks"} locally constant infinity-stacks
            in the higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
            encoded by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
            now become coverings that are constant on
            %em small
            scales. This is the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism"} étale morphism
            as being a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
            with a condition of smallness on its fibers.
          %p
            Hence we find that this further determination is that of the moment of
