              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat moment
              of this as follows.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi θ
                          %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G
                    \\stackrel{\theta_G}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}G
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\flat \mathbf{B}G
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbf{B}G
                    \\,.
            %p
              This double homotopy fiber
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_G
              has the interpretation of being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h5#differential_cohomology Differential cohomology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔾
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+%E2%88%9E-group"} abelian ∞-group
            type. The group of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+and+phase+space+in+physics"} phases
          %p
            This being abelian just means that there is specified a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi 𝔾
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} \mathbb{G}
            and an equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔾
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Ω
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi 𝔾
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}\simeq \Omega \mathbf{B} \mathbb{G}
            with its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 0
                  %mi 𝔾
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi 𝔾
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^0 \mathbb{G} \coloneqq \mathbb{G}
            we have inductively that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi 𝔾
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n \mathbb{G}
            is itself equipped with the structure of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+%E2%88%9E-group"} abelian ∞-group
          %p
            For the present purpose we will assume in addition that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔾
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated"} 0-truncated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+filtration"} Hodge filtration
              is a compatible system of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtrations"} filtrations
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi 𝔾
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat \mathbf{B}^2\mathbb{G}
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mo →
                    %mo ♭
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^{2}_{cl}
                    \\to
                    
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    \\flat_{dR} \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{G}
                    \\to
                    \\flat \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{G}
                    \\,.
            %p
              with 0-truncated extensive
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Ω
                        %mi cl
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Omega}^{2}_{cl}
          #BGconn.num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+filtration"} Hodge filtration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}_{conn}
              for the homotopy fiber product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi conn
                    %mo ≔
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ♭
                          %mi dR
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mn 2
                        %mi 𝔾
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}_{conn}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}\underset{\flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}^2\mathbb{G}}{\times} \mathbf{\Omega}^2_{cl}
            %p
              of the Maurer-Cartan form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi 𝔾
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_{\mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}}
              with the last Hodge filtration stage.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              The decomposition of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}_{conn}
              into its
              = succeed "-moments" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mo ♭
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (&amp;#643;, \overline{\flat})
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheHexagon"}
              reproduces the defining Cartesian square of def.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BGconn"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Ω
                              %mi cl
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔾
                              %mi conn
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mi 𝔾
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi 𝔾
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %mi B
                            %mi 𝔾
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mi 𝔾
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{\Omega}^2_{cl}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}_{conn}
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                    \\flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}^2\mathbb{G}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}\mathbb{G} &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;  \flat_{dR}B \mathbb{G}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; B \mathbb{G}
                    }
          %h5#WZWTerms WZW terms
          %p A map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
