          %p
            There are no non-trivial judgements with (a delooping of)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            as the subject and (a delooping of)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0|1}
            as the predicate. But there turn out to be some exceptional judgements with subject
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0|q}
            and predicate
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi d
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^d \mathbb{R}
          %p
            By example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PrincipalBundlesAsJudgements"}
            this leads to the deduction of the object which is the homotopy fibers of the corresponding maps. From these one obtains further judgements, then further objects, and so forth. This way a “bouquet” of objects is induced from the initial ones.
          %p
            We now discuss how this bouquet first of all yields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            and then further the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} extended super Minkowski spacetimes
            arising from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
            condensates (
            %a{:href => "#FSS"}> FSS
            ).
          %h6#minkowski_spacetime Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            Consider first the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0|1}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_13 Remark
            %p This is the unique 0-truncated object which is
            %ol
              %li
                %p purely negative to bosonic moment;
              %li
                %p purely opposite to bosonic moment;
            %p in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\e(\mathbb{R}^{0|1})\simeq \mathbb{R}^{0|1}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ⇉
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\stackrel{\rightrightarrows}{\mathbb{R}^{0|1}} \simeq \ast
                    \\,.
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0|1}
            (and the other objects obtained in a moment) are contractible as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+groups"} super Lie groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Est+isomorphism"} van Est isomorphism
            to conveniently discuss them as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}
            as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            is freely generated from a
            = succeed "-bigraded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,odd)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\theta
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi d
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1})
                  \=
                  \\left(
                  \\wedge^\bullet \langle d\theta \rangle, d_{CE} = 0
                  \\right)
                  \\,.
          %p It is evident that
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_20 Proposition
            %p
              The second
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^{2}(\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}, \mathbb{R})
                    \=
                    \\mathbb{R}
            %p represented by the 2-cocycles of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi θ
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %mi θ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d\theta\wedge d\theta
                    \\in CE(\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1})
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} Lie algebra extension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 1
                            %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R}^{1|\mathbf{1}}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^{0|1}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^1 \mathbb{R}
                    }
            %p
              classified by this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+group"} super translation group
              in 1-dimension.
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline"} worldline
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superparticle"} superparticle
          %p There are no further non-trivial cocycles here giving further extensions.
          %p
            Hence next consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            of the initial superpoint with itself.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^{0|2}
                  \=
                  \\mathbb{R}^{0|1}\times \mathbb{R}^{0|1}
                  \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_14 Remark
            %p
              This is still purely of negative bosonic moment in that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e(\mathbb{R}^{0|2}) \simeq \mathbb{R}^{0|2}
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompletenessOfOppositionsInSuperFormalSmoothTypes"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mn 2
                      %mo ⇉
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\stackrel{\rightrightarrows}{\mathbb{R}^{0|2}}
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{D}(1)
            %p
              is the first-order
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+interval"} infinitesimal interval
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+dual+numbers"}> algebra of dual numbers
              ”).
          #3dSuperMinkowskiSpacetime.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_21 Proposition
            %p
              The second
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0\vert 2}
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^2(\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 2}, \mathbb{R})
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{R}^3
            %p represented by the cocycles of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 11
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 22
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 12
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_{11}
                    \\,
                    d\theta_1 \wedge d\theta_1
                    +
                    a_{22}
                    \\,
                    d\theta_2 \wedge d\theta_2
                    +
                    a_{12}
                    \\,
                    d\theta_1 \wedge d\theta_2
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group+extension"} extension
              classified by this
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R}^{2,1|\mathbf{2}}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^{0|2}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B} \mathbb{R}^3
                    }
            %p
              is 3-dimensional
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              This follows by inspection of the real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representations"} spin representations
              in dimension 3, see the details spelled out at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/spin%20representation#RealSpinorRepsIn3d"} spin representation – via division algebras – Example d=3
          %p
            Now the old
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            gives:
          .num_pro
            %h6#proposition_22 Proposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^3(\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert \mathbf{2}}) = \mathbb{R}
            %p
              represented by the 3-cocycle which, as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+differential+form"} left invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+form"} super differential form
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert \mathbf{2}}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+term"} WZW term
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
              for the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+1-brane+in+3d"} super 1-brane in 3d
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔰𝔱𝔯𝔦𝔫𝔤
                              %mrow
                                %mi het
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mi on
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %msub
                                  %mi G
                                  %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathfrak{string}_{het \, on \, G_2}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert \mathbf{2}}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{R}
                    }
          %p
            A definite globalization, of this 3-cocycle over a
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{3\vert \mathbf{2}}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DefiniteGlobalizationofWZWTerm"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            is a bundle of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
            and that the cocycle extends to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+form"} definite form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            (or rather its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+cover"} double cover
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_23 Proposition
            %p
              The joint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer"} stabilizer
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert 2})
              of the Lie bracket and the 3-cocycle is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pin+group"} pin group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Pin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pin(2,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(2,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+cover"} double cover
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(2,1)
          %p
            This is one special case of a more general statement which we come to as prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilizerOfSupersymmetryJointWith3Cocycle"}
            below.
          %p
            Consider then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert 4}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mn 4
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mn 2
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert 4}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{R}^{0 \vert 2} &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \mathbb{R}^{0\vert 2}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B} \mathbb{R}^3
                  }
                  \\,.
          #4dSuperMinkowskiSpacetime.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_24 Proposition
            %p
              There is a 1-dimensional space of
              = succeed "-invariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(2,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 2
                          %mo +
                          %mover
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert \mathbf{2} + \overline{\mathbf{2}}}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} Lie algebra extension
              classified by that is 4d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 3
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mn 4
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo +
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R}^{3,1\vert 4}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^{2,1\vert \mathbf{2}+{\mathbf{2}}}
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}\mathbb{R}
                    }
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p
              By inspection of the real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representations"} spin representations
              in dimension 4.
          %p
            Now the old
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            gives:
          #TheStringIn4d.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_25 Proposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 3
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^4(\mathbb{R}^{3,1\vert \mathbf{4}}) = \mathbb{R}
            %p
              represented by the 4-cocycle which, as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+differential+form"} left invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+form"} super differential form
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 3
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{3,1\vert \mathbf{2}}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+term"} WZW term
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
              for the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+2-brane+in+4d"} super 2-brane in 4d
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝔪
                            %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝔟𝔯𝔞𝔫𝔢
                              %mrow
                                %mi on
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %msub
                                  %mi G
                                  %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 3
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mn 4
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 3
                            %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathfrak{m}2\mathfrak{brane}_{on\,G_2}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^{3,1\vert  \mathbf{4} }
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^3 \mathbb{R}
                    }
                    \\,.
          %h6#lorentz_symmetry Lorentz symmetry
          %p
            Notice that so far we have obtained 3-dimensional and 4-dimensional Minkowski spacetime and the WZW-term for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane"} membrane
            propagating on it without assuming knowledge of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/odd+line"} odd line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0|1}
            and we have simply investigated their cohomology.
          %p
            The following proposition shows that the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+cover"} universal cover
            by the pseudo-Riemannian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            is
            %em deduced
            from this.
          #StabilizerOfSupersymmetryJointWith3Cocycle.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_26 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1,N}
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 4
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 6
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 10
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \{3,4,6,10\}
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in \Omega^{3}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
              the corresponding 3-form characterizing the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super-1-brane
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"}> superstring
              ) in this dimension, according to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
              \. Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
              of both the super Lie bracket and the cocycle is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+group"} Spin group
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Stab
                      %mrow
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Stab_{GL(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})}([-,-], \phi)
                    \\simeq
                    Spin(d-1,1) \hookrightarrow GL(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_9 Proof
            %p
              It is clear that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
              fixes the cocycle, and by the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
              it preserves the bracket. Therefore it remains to be seen that the Spin group already exhausts the stabiizer group of bracket and cocycle. For that observe that the 3-cocycle is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\psi,\phi, v) \mapsto \eta( [\psi,\phi], v )
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta(-,-)
              is the given
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+metric"} Minkowski metric
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [-,-]\colon S \otimes S\to V
            %p
              is surjective. This imples that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in GL(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
              preserves both the bracket and the cocycle for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi, \phi \in S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
              to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta( [g(\psi),g(\phi)], g(v) )
                    \=
                    \\eta( g([\psi,\phi]), g(v) )
                    \=
                    \\eta( [\psi,\phi], v )
            %p
              then it preserves the Minkowski metric for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w,v
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
