          %ol
            %li
              %p further determinations of being (these are the transitions within each book of the system)
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    second order unity of opposites, coming from an
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
                    going vertically. This is progression by opposition. The name of the given second order unity is indicated in the middle of these squares.
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aufhebung"}> Aufhebung
                    , by which a new
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modality"} adjoint modality
                    appears whose
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+types"} modal types
                    include the modal types of the previous stage, indicated by a vertical inclusion sign
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∨
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee
            %li
              %p reiteration of the system of adjoint modalities (these are the transitions between the books of the system)
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    First there is the plain system of modalities, starting from the smallest subcategories
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ∅
                          %mo ⊣
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \dashv \ast
                    and ending at the maximal subcategories, the whole category itself
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi id
                            %mo ⊣
                            %mi id
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id \dashv id
                %li
                  %p
                    Then, passing to the
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em Essence
                    %em appears
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em reflected
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+extensionality"} propositional extensionality
                %li
                  %p
                    Next, passing to
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em Nature
                    %em externalizes
                    or
                    %em represents
                    itself via a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
                    (as discussed at
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %em
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory"} relation between type theory and category theory
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)
                    re-appears as its representation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(-)
                    in that model.
