          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+%28in+computer+science%29"} monads in computer science
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+monad"} function monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [W,-]
            is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reader+monad"} reader monad
            (notably in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haskell"} Haskell
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programming+language"} programming language
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
