          %h3#relation_to_logic_mathematics_and_physics Relation to Logic, Mathematics and Physics
          %p
            Comments on the general aim of a fundamental logic based on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dialectic"} dialectic
            are in
          %ul
            %li#Wandschneider99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+Wandschneider"}> Dieter Wandschneider
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Dialektik als Letztbegründung der Logik
              %em Festschrift für Sok-Zin Lim
              Seoul 1999, 255–278 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.philosophie.rwth-aachen.de/global/show_document.asp?id=aaaaaaaaaabpltw"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Related discussion in view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimals"} infinitesimals
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Cohen83
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Cohen"}> Hermann Cohen
              ,
              %em Das Prinzip der Infinitesimal-Methode und seine Geschichte
              , Berlin 1883. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.gleichsatz.de/b-u-t/archiv/Cohen/hc-infinit1.html"}> html
              )
          %p
            Reflections by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Hilbert"} David Hilbert
            on the claim that laws of physics may follow from pure concepts, in view of more modern developments in physics (cf.
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
