          %h3#ReferencesConceptLogicAsTypeTheory Concept logic as Type theory
          %p
            The idea that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            are (mathematical)
            %em concepts
            or
            %em notions
            (i.e. “Begriffe”, as in the
            %a{:href => "#Dictionary"} formalization dictionary
            above ) is arguably implicit in the original
          %ul
            %li#MartinLoef73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em An intuitionistic theory of types: predicative part
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.131.926"} web
          %p where it says in section 1.1:
          %blockquote
            %p
              Every mathematical object is of a certain type [] a type is well defined if we understand (or
              %em grasp
              to use a word favoured by Kreisel 1970) what it means to be an object of that type.
          %p and
          %ul
            %li#MartinLoef90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A path from logic to metaphysics
              = succeed "," do
                %em Nuovi problemi della logica e della filosofia della scienza
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/michaelt/martin-lof/raw/master/pdfs/A-path-from-logic-to-metaphysics-1991.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            where it says on p. 1 (to be read with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            in mind):
          %blockquote
            %p …by saying that a concept has existence, I mean that there exists an object which falls under the concept. So to say that a proposition is true is the same as to say that the concept ‘proof of the proposition’ has existence…
          %p and
          %ul
            %li#MartinLoef93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Philosophical aspects of intuitionistic type theory
          %p where he was recorded as saying
          %blockquote
            %p
              There is no question of talking of an object of type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              unless
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              is a type, so the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              here is the universal general concept under which
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              = succeed "," do
                %em Des catégories aux types : un itinéraire en mathématiques appliquées
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://pboldini.free.fr/Papers/mathmu.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The explicit statement “a type is a concept” appears for instance (referring both to types of mathematical objects as well as to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+types"} data types
            in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computer+science"} computer science
          %ul
            %li#Sale77
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+Sale"}> Arthur Sale
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Primitive data types
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://eprints.utas.edu.au/139/1/PrimitiveData.pdf"} pdf
          %p The explicit statement “a type is a ‘mathematical’ concept” appears on p. 6 of
          %ul
            %li#Sergeraert94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Sergeraert"}> Francis Sergeraert
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The computability problem in algebraic topology
              %a{:href => "http://www-fourier.ujf-grenoble.fr/~sergerar/Papers/Advances.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and with explicit reference to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            in
          %ul
            %li#Primiero08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giuseppe+Primiero"}> Giuseppe Primiero
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Information and knowledge: A constructive type-theoretical approach
          %p where it says on page 129:
          %blockquote
            %p
              %em> Types are general concepts
              \: This statement represents the main conceptual basis of the whole idea of using CTT [constructive type theory] as a language to formalize knowledge processes.
          %p as well as
          %ul
            %li#Asher11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Asher"}> Nicholas Asher
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Web of Words, Lexical Meaning in Context
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.phil.pku.edu.cn/cllct/ann_attachments/asher_webofwords.pdf"} pdf
          %p where it says on pages 37/38:
          %blockquote
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              this leads us to the hypothesis that types are concepts.
          %p
            With explicit reference to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            the proposal that “type” should be read as a “concept” is voiced in
          %ul
            %li#LadymanPresnel14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Ladyman"}> James Ladyman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stuart+Presnell"} Stuart Presnell
              = succeed "," do
                %em Does Homotopy Type Theory Provide a Foundation for Mathematics?
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://philsci-archive.pitt.edu/11143/"} PhilArchive
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/bjps/axw006"} doi.org/10.1093/bjps/axw006
          %p
            Hence the types of type theory may be thought of as a formalization of concepts. On the other hand, concepts have famously been identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicates"} predicates
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aristotelian+logic"} Aristotelian logic
          %blockquote
            %p#Kant1871A69B94
              %em Concepts … serve as predicates of possible judgements.
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Critique+of+Pure+Reason"} Critique of Pure Reason
              A69/B94)
          %h3#ReferencesFormalizations Formalizations
          %p
            Proposals for formalizing some of Hegel’s thoughts in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            may be identified in
          %ul
            %li#Grassmann1844
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Grassmann"}> Hermann Grassmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ausdehnungslehre"} Ausdehnungslehre
          %p and, apparently following this, according to
          %ul
            %li#Lawvere95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A new branch of mathematics, “The Ausdehnungslehre of 1844,” and other works. Open Court (1995), Translated by Lloyd C. Kannenberg, with foreword by Albert C. Lewis
              %em Historia Mathematica Volume 32, Issue 1, February 2005, Pages 99–106
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S031508600400059X"}> publisher
              )
          %p
            proposals for formalization of Hegel’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+logic"} objective logic
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            have been put forward by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"} William Lawvere
            in several places, for instance in
          %ul
            %li#LawvereComo
              %p#Lawvere91
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+Thoughts+on+the+Future+of+Category+Theory"} Some Thoughts on the Future of Category Theory
                in A. Carboni, M. Pedicchio, G. Rosolini,
                %em Category Theory
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Como"} Proceedings of the International Conference held in Como
            %li#LawvereLauterEinsen
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohesive+Toposes+and+Cantor%27s+%22lauter+Einsen%22"} Cohesive Toposes and Cantor's "lauter Einsen"
            %li#Lawvere94b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tools+for+the+advancement+of+objective+logic"}> Tools for the advancement of objective logic
                    \: closed categories and toposes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gonzalo+Reyes"} Gonzalo Reyes
                (Eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Logical Foundations of Cognition
              %p pages 43-56, 1994.
            %li#LawvereMotion
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toposes+of+laws+of+motion"} Toposes of laws of motion
                , transcript of a talk in Montreal, Sept. 1997 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.acsu.buffalo.edu/~wlawvere/ToposMotion.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Lawvere92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                %em Categories of space and quantity
                in J. Echeverria et al (eds.),
                %em The Space of mathematics
                , de Gruyter, Berlin, New York, pages 14-30, 1992.
          %p Related commentary is in
          %ul
            %li#Rodin14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Rodin"}> Andrei Rodin
              , section 5.8
              %em Categorical Logic and Hegelian Dialectics
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Axiomatic Method and Category Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1210.1478"} arXiv:1210.1478
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783319004037"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-00404-4
          %p
            Discussion of formalization of the topics of the “subjective logic” within
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            include
          %ul
            %li#MartinLoef96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the Meanings of the Logical Constants and the Justifications of the Logical Laws
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://docenti.lett.unisi.it/files/4/1/1/6/martinlof4.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            which gives a detailed discussion of the term
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgement"} judgement
            as used in the history
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy"} philosophy
            and then in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
          %p
            Texts on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
            which comment on the circularity (or not) of foundations include
          %ul
            %li#Trimble13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"}> Todd Trimble
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/toddtrimble/published/Notes+on+predicate+logic"} Notes on predicate logic
          %p
            The formalization of
            %em Schluss
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} natural deduction
            originates in
          %ul
            %li#Gentzen35
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerhard+Gentzen"}> Gerhard Gentzen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Untersuchungen über das logische Schließen
              %em Mathematische Zeitschrift
              39(1), Springer-Verlag 1935.
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BF01201353"} http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BF01201353
              (English translation
              %em Investigations into Logical Deduction
              in Szabo)
          %p
            Further references referred to in the context of the formalization discussed
            %a{:href => "#FormalizationText"} above
            include the following:
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V%C3%B6lkl"} Michael Völkl
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential cohomology theories as sheaves of spectra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3188"} arXiv:1311.3188
            %li#FSS
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
            %li#Johnstone02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"}> Sketches of an Elephant – A Topos Theory Compendium
                  , Oxford 2002.
            %li#Lawvere07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                %em Axiomatic cohesion
                Theory and Applications of Categories, Vol. 19, No. 3, 2007, pp. 41–49. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/19/3/19-03abs.html"}> web
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/19/3/19-03.pdf"} pdf
            %li#NSS
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles+--+theory%2C+presentations+and+applications"} Principal ∞-Bundles – General theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.0248"} arXiv:1207.0248
            %li#dcct
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
            %li#PalmeReyesMacnamaraReyes94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marie+La+Palme+Reyes"}> Marie La Palme Reyes
                , John Macnamara,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gonzalo+Reyes"} Gonzalo Reyes
                ,
                %em Functoriality and Grammatical Role in Syllogisms
                , Notre Dame J. Formal Logic
                %strong 35
                no.1 (1994) pp.41-66. (
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ndjfl/1040609293"}> Euclid
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/download/pdf_1/euclid.ndjfl/1040609293"} pdf
            %li#Pagnan10
              %p
                Ruggero Pagnan,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A diagrammatic calculus of syllogisms
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1001.1707"} arXiv:1001.1707
            %li#Shulman12a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Univalence for inverse diagrams and homotopy canonicity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.3253"} arXiv:1203.3253
            %li#Shulman12b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
                ,
                %em Inductive and higher inductive types
                (2012) (
                %a{:href => "https://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/hottminicourse2012/04induction.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Shulman14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/homotopytypetheory/show/model+of+type+theory+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} model of type theory in an (infinity,1)-topos
            %li#UFP13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
          %p
            Another proposal for formalizing dialectics, with emphasis on using
            = succeed "-typed" do
              %em un
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Uwe+Petersen"} Uwe Petersen
          %ul
            %li#Petersen09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Uwe+Petersen"}> Uwe Petersen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em 35 Thesen zur Grundlegung einer formalen dialektischen Logik — nebst Kommentaren
              %strong 4
              (2009) 125–207 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://asfpg.de/english/17303/Jahrbuecher/JB09/jb09-petersen.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
